## Checked and found clean

- **`well-formed-utf16?`** (`:250-267`) is a correct reimplementation: lone low surrogate → false; high surrogate without a following low surrogate → false; pairs skipped. `code-unit-at` per-host (`:171-175`) matches.
- **No regression from the `:str` reroute**: for a *valid* `:str`, `(encode-scalar x)` == `(framed :string x)`, and for nil both paths yield `(framed :string "")` — bytes unchanged (`:503` vs old `(framed :string (or x ""))`).
- **`scope-defect` re-check of `nonneg-int?` depth/position** is dead-but-harmless (negative depths are already rejected earlier by `operand-kind-rule`, per the test at `:58-60`).
- **No stray callers**: `all-body-chains`/`walk-body` are only reached from `scope-defect`; the changed return shape is fully propagated.
- **Golden bytes**: `encode-image` is descriptor-independent, so the four byte strings are provably untouched by P3-4; the four re-pinned hashes are self-consistent (each 64-hex, asserted against live `image-hash` on every lane, so any half-update would fail the suite on all three hosts). I did not recompute the sha256 preimages (read-only, no run) — correctness rests on the suite, which the implementer reports clean for JVM+CLJS.
- **`#?` hygiene on the new code**: `host-double?`'s `:clj`/`:default` split is safe for CLJD/CLJS (no `:clj` fallthrough); `nonneg-int?`'s `:cljs`/`:default` has no `:clj` branch and defaults to the portable rule; the ratio range-check stays inside `:default` so Dart/JS never resolve `numerator`/`denominator`.

Findings only; no file edited.
